.\" Man page for HSYNC — file synchronization client
.\" =====================================================================

.TH HSYNC 1 "2026-10-06" "hsync 1.0" "User Commands"
.
.\" ---------------------------------------------------------------------
.SH NAME
hsync \- file synchronization client (Server and P2P modes)
.
.\" ---------------------------------------------------------------------
.SH SYNOPSIS
.SY hsync
.B server
.OP \-b NAME
.RB [ hostname [:PORT] ]
.OP \-\-port PORT
.OP \-p DIR
.RI [ OPTIONS ]
.YS
.
.SY hsync
.B p2p
.OP \-b NAME
.OP \-p DIR
.RI [ BOOTNODE [:PORT] ]
.OP \-\-port PORT
.RI [ OPTIONS ]
.YS
.
.SY hsync
.B trust
.BI peer | bootnode | server
.RI [ OPTIONS ]
.YS
.
.SY hsync
.B \-\-help
.YS
.
.SY hsync
.B \-\-version
.YS
.
.\" ---------------------------------------------------------------------
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B hsync
keeps directories in sync across machines and NAS devices.
It supports two operating modes, selected by the subcommand:
.
.TP 4
\(bu
.BR "Server Mode" " (" hsync " " server ):
Clients connect to a central HSYNC server.
The server hosts shared directories ("buckets") and coordinates
synchronization between all connected clients.
.
.TP 4
\(bu
.BR "p2p Mode (P2P)" " (" hsync " " p2p ):
Clients discover each other automatically via mDNS on the local network.
One peer is elected
.B master
and the others become
.BR slaves .
No central server is required. p2p traffic is always HTTPS/WSS
(there is no plaintext transport). Writes are authorized by a shared secret
.RB ( HSYNC_P2P_KEY );
a keyless p2p group is read-only.
.
.SS Features
\(bu Real-time file watching with
.I inotify
\& (Linux)
.br
\(bu Compression of transferred data via zstd
.br
\(bu Exact-hash peer-assisted p2p downloads with automatic master fallback
.br
\(bu Bandwidth throttling per transfer direction
.br
\(bu Exclusion patterns (.hsyncignore, gitignore-style)
.br
\(bu Dry-run preview mode
.br
\(bu Structured JSON-Lines status output for GUI integration
.
.\" ---------------------------------------------------------------------
.SH OPTIONS
.B hsync
options are organised by subcommand: options shared by both subcommands,
subcommand-specific options, and global options typed before the subcommand.
.
.\" --- Required ---
.SS Required (both subcommands)
.TP
.BR \-b ", " \-\-bucket =\fINAME\fP
Remote bucket name. Alphanumeric characters, hyphens, and underscores
are allowed (not at the beginning or end).
This option is mandatory.
.
.\" --- Server subcommand ---
.SS Server subcommand
.TP
.BI hostname [\fI:PORT\fP]
Remote server host or IP
.RI ( server\.example\.com ),
optionally with a port
.RI ( server\.example\.com\fI:443\fP ).
HTTPS is always used; the port defaults to 9753 (the hsync\-server
default) and a reverse proxy on 443 is selected with
.BR \-\-port .
Can also be configured as a full URL via the
.B HSYNC_SERVER
environment variable. Required for
.B hsync server
unless
.B HSYNC_SERVER
is set.
.TP
.BR \-\-port =\fIPORT\fP
Remote server port (default: 9753). Requires
.BR hostname .
Mutually exclusive with a port given in
.BI hostname [\fI:PORT\fP] .
.TP
.B \-\-insecure
Skip SSL/TLS certificate verification (not recommended).
.TP
.BR \-\-ca\-cert =\fIFILE\fP
Path to a custom CA certificate file for self-signed server certificates.
.TP
.BR \-\-server\-fingerprint =\fIFINGERPRINT\fP
Pin the sync\-server certificate fingerprint
.RI ( sha256:<hex> " or bare hex)."
May be repeated (up to two) for a rotation window; implies
.BR strict .
.TP
.B \-\-server\-tofu
Trust the sync\-server certificate on first use (TOFU); a later mismatch is
refused. Implies
.BR accept\-new .
.TP
.BR \-\-server\-trust =\fIPOLICY\fP
Sync\-server TLS trust policy:
.BR chain
(default: standard CA validation),
.BR ask
(confirm an unknown fingerprint on a terminal, fail closed without one),
.BR accept\-new ,
.B strict
or
.BR none .
.TP
.BR \-\-api\-key\-fd =\fIFD\fP
Read the API key from the given file descriptor. This is a hidden option
intended for secure passing of secrets from a parent process.
.
.\" --- Sync ---
.SS Sync (both subcommands)
.TP
.BR \-p ", " \-\-path =\fIDIR\fP
Local directory to synchronize (default: current directory).
.TP
.B \-\-once
Run a single sync cycle and exit. Without
.B \-\-once
the client runs continuously (daemon mode, the default): it keeps the
connection open, syncs changes in real time, and retries an unreachable
server indefinitely instead of exiting. In p2p mode it runs one slave sync
cycle and exits, and a run that is still alone when
.B \-\-discovery\-timeout
expires exits with code
.B 5
instead of serving as a lone master; a master that is serving live peers
stays continuous regardless.
.TP
.BR \-i ", " \-\-interval =\fISEC\fP
Force a full re-scan every
.I SEC
seconds in continuous mode (range: 20\(en3600).
.TP
.BR \-\-retry\-delay =\fISEC\fP
Base interval (seconds) for the full-jitter exponential reconnect backoff:
each consecutive failed reconnect doubles the upper bound, capped at 60 s,
with a uniform random delay in that window. The client never gives up.
When auto-tuning is enabled (default), the base is derived from RTT if not
set explicitly. Range: 1\(en60.
.TP
.BR \-\-stability\-delay =\fISEC\fP
Seconds a file must stay unchanged before it is uploaded
(default: 5; range: 1\(en60).
Files whose modification time is already older than this
are uploaded immediately. After a writer close
(\fIIN_CLOSE_WRITE\fP) a 0.3s re-check is used instead.
.TP
.BR \-\-max\-wait\-timeout =\fISEC\fP
Maximum time to wait for a file to stabilize (default:
.BR 120 ;
range: 10\(en3600).
.TP
.BR \-\-subdir =\fIPATH\fP
Sync only files within this subdirectory path.
.TP
.BR \-n ", " \-\-dry\-run
Show what would be done without making any changes.
.TP
.B \-\-ignore\-delete
Do not propagate file deletions. Useful for backup scenarios
where you never want remote files deleted when they disappear locally.
.TP
.BR \-\-sync\-direction =\fIDIR\fP
Sync direction. One of:
.BR bidirectional " (default),"
.BR upload\-only ", or"
.BR download\-only .
.TP
.BR \-\-limit\-upload =\fIRATE\fP
Maximum upload bandwidth
.RI ( e.g. " 1MB ", " 500KB ").
0 = unlimited.
.TP
.BR \-\-limit\-download =\fIRATE\fP
Maximum download bandwidth (same format as above).
.TP
.B \-\-no\-compression
Disable zstd compression for file transfers.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-delta
Disable rsync-style delta transfer (block-level sync) for large files with
small changes. When disabled, all files are transferred in full. Delta transfer
is enabled by default and automatically reduces bandwidth for files \(>= 256 KB
(server mode) or \(>= 1 MB (p2p mode) when both peers support it.
.TP
.BR \-\-delta\-min\-file\-size =\fIBYTES\fP
Minimum file size in bytes for delta transfer in server mode (default:
.BR 262144 ,
256 KB). Files smaller than this threshold are always transferred in full.
.TP
.BR \-\-delta\-min\-file\-size\-p2p =\fIBYTES\fP
Minimum file size in bytes for delta transfer in p2p mode (default:
.BR 1048576 ,
1 MB). p2p mode uses a higher threshold because the bandwidth savings are
less significant on fast local networks.
.TP
.BR \-\-min\-free\-disk\-space =\fIMB\fP
Minimum free disk space in MB before sync is paused
(default:
.BR 500 ;
range: 0\(en100000, 0 = disabled).
.TP
.BR \-\-ignore\-pattern =\fIPATTERN\fP
Extra gitignore-style pattern. May be repeated for multiple patterns.
Layered on
.B .hsyncignore
(if present in the synced directory).
.TP
.BR \-\-mass\-delete\-guard " / " \-\-no\-mass\-delete\-guard
Enable or disable the mass-deletion safety guard. When enabled (default:
.BR on ),
a cycle that would delete more files than the configured thresholds is paused
instead.
.TP
.BR \-\-mass\-delete\-threshold =\fIN\fP
Absolute number of deletions per synchronisation cycle that trips the
mass-deletion guard (default:
.BR 50 ;
set to 0 to disable the absolute threshold).
.TP
.BR \-\-mass\-delete\-percent =\fIPCT\fP
Percentage of local files whose deletion trips the mass-deletion guard
(default:
.BR 50 ;
set to 0 to disable the percentage threshold).
.TP
.BR \-\-max\-concurrent\-transfers =\fIN\fP
Maximum number of concurrent file transfers (default:
.BR 5 ;
range: 1\(en20).
.TP
.BR \-\-max\-inbound\-size =\fIMB\fP
Maximum size in MB of a single inbound file (download or received p2p upload),
enforced as an absolute cap on top of the peer-declared size (default:
.BR 10240 ,
10 GB; 0 = disabled).
.TP
.B \-\-no\-autotune
Disable auto-tuning of timeout, retry, and concurrency. When set, the
client uses static defaults for all auto-tunable parameters instead of
deriving them from the runtime environment. Equivalent to setting
.BR HSYNC_AUTOTUNE=false .
.TP
.BR \-\-http\-timeout =\fISEC\fP
HTTP request timeout in seconds. When auto-tuning is enabled (default), the
timeout is derived from measured network latency if not set explicitly.
Applies to server REST requests and, in p2p mode, to the master's HTTPS
transport. Range: 1\(en300.
.TP
.BR \-\-events\-json\-fd =\fIFD\fP
Write structured JSON-Lines status events to the given file descriptor.
Hidden option intended for GUI integration.
.
.\" --- p2p subcommand ---
.SS p2p subcommand
.TP
.BR BOOTNODE [\fI:PORT\fP]
Optional bootnode host for cross-network peer discovery: a bare hostname/IPv4,
a bracketed IPv6 literal, or a
.IR HOST : PORT
pair (the QUIC scheme is implied); omit it to stay on mDNS only.
.TP
.BR \-\-listen\-port =\fIPORT\fP
Port to listen on when acting as p2p master (default: 0 = auto).
.TP
.BR \-\-port =\fIPORT\fP
UDP (QUIC) port of the remote bootnode (default: 443). Only meaningful with
.BR BOOTNODE ;
without it,
.B \-\-port
is refused rather than ignored. Mutually exclusive with a port given in
.BR BOOTNODE [\fI:PORT\fP] .
.TP
.B \-\-upnp
Map the master TCP port with UPnP (opt\-in; off by default). Without a bootnode
the flag has no effect (mDNS discovery stays on the local network).
.TP
.BI \-\-bootnode\-fingerprint\fP= FINGERPRINT
Pin the bootnode certificate fingerprint (canonical
.I sha256:<hex>
or bare hex); repeatable up to two values for a rotation window. Refused
without a
.BR BOOTNODE .
Selects the
.I strict
trust policy.
.TP
.B \-\-bootnode\-tofu
Trust the bootnode certificate on first use (accept-new); a later mismatch is
refused as a possible man-in-the-middle. Selects the
.I accept-new
trust policy.
.TP
.BI \-\-bootnode\-trust\fP= POLICY
Bootnode TLS trust policy. One of:
.RS
.TP
.I ask
(default) Prompt on a terminal to accept an unknown fingerprint, then remember
it; refuse a changed one. Without a terminal the client fails closed.
.TP
.I accept-new
Pin the first sighting silently (same as
.BR \-\-bootnode\-tofu ).
.TP
.I strict
Require a pin (same as
.BR \-\-bootnode\-fingerprint ).
.TP
.I none
No verification (loopback/tests only; same as an unpinned insecure link).
.RE
.IP
The decision is remembered in the known-hosts store (see
.BR HSYNC_BOOTNODE_TRUST_FILE );
manage it with
.BR "hsync trust bootnode" .
.TP
.BR \-\-discovery\-timeout =\fISEC\fP
Time to wait for initial p2p peer discovery
(default:
.BR 0 ;
wait indefinitely, matching the server-mode default of retrying an
unreachable server forever). In a one-shot run
.RB ( \-\-once )
this wait is the run's whole budget: a client that is still alone when it
expires exits with code
.B 5
instead of acting as a peer-less master.
.TP
.BR \-\-group =\fIGROUP\fP
Group name for p2p peer filtering. Only peers with the same group
will discover each other.
.TP
.B \-\-force\-master
Force this client to always act as master in p2p mode.
.TP
.B \-\-never\-master
Never become master in p2p mode (always remain a slave).
.TP
.B \-\-require\-pairing
Strict pairing: refuse a first-seen p2p master certificate until it is
confirmed out of band (disables Trust-On-First-Use auto-pinning).
.TP
.B \-\-no\-peer\-download
Disable peer-assisted p2p downloads for this run. By default, large full-file
downloads may use a verified continuous slave before falling back to the master.
.TP
.B \-\-allow\-unauthenticated\-writes
Dangerous explicit opt-in: allow LAN mutations when no shared p2p key is
configured. Without this option, no-key p2p groups are read-only.
.TP
.B \-\-allow\-unauthenticated\-p2p
Explicitly acknowledge a keyless p2p run: peers are not authenticated and reads
are open to anyone who can reach the node. Without it (or the writes opt-in) the
client asks for confirmation on a terminal and fails closed otherwise.
.TP
.BR \-\-p2p\-key\-fd =\fIFD\fP
Read the p2p shared secret from the given file descriptor. Hidden option.
.
.\" --- Output ---
.SS Output (both subcommands)
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-verbose
Enable verbose (debug) output.
.TP
.BR \-q ", " \-\-quiet
Suppress all output.
.TP
.BR \-\-log\-file =\fIFILE\fP
Write output to
.I FILE
instead of the terminal.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-color
Disable colored output.
.
.\" --- General ---
.SS General (both subcommands)
.TP
.BR \-\-allow\-deletions
Accept the deletion risk: a download-only sync may delete local-only files to
mirror the source.
.TP
.BR \-\-env\-file =\fIPATH\fP
Load environment variables from a file (KEY=VALUE, one per line).
.
.\" --- Global options ---
.SS Global options
The following are parent options, typed before the subcommand:
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Show version and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-capabilities\-json
Print the binary's capabilities document as JSON and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-help\-symbols
Show a legend of the output symbols.
.
.\" --- Trust management ---
.SS Trust management (known peers / known hosts / known servers)
The client pins self-signed certificate fingerprints in three SSH-style stores:
the p2p known-peers store (keyed by
.IR device-id|bucket ),
the bootnode known-hosts store (keyed by
.IR host:port )
and the sync-server known-hosts store (keyed by
.IR host:port ).
All three are managed through one
.B hsync trust
namespace; verify a fingerprint out of band before pinning it.
.TP
.B "hsync trust peer {list,add,remove} [\-\-json]"
Manage the p2p known-peers store (identities are
.IR device-id|bucket ).
.TP
.B "hsync trust bootnode {list,show,add,remove,fingerprint} [\-\-json]"
Manage the bootnode known-hosts store.
.B fingerprint
prints a node's certificate fingerprint without trusting it.
.TP
.B "hsync trust server {list,show,add,remove,fingerprint} [\-\-json]"
Manage the sync-server known-hosts store.
.B fingerprint
prints a server's certificate fingerprint without trusting it.
.TP
.BR "hsync trust \fISTORE\fP add \fIid fingerprint\fP [\-\-port PORT] [\-\-bucket NAME]"
Pin a fingerprint (accepts
.I sha256:<hex>
or bare hex; exits non-zero on an invalid fingerprint).
.TP
.BR "hsync trust \fISTORE\fP remove \fIid\fP [\-\-port PORT] [\-\-bucket NAME]"
Forget a pin (like
.BR "ssh\-keygen \-R" ).
.PP
.B list
prints one entry per line;
.B \-\-json
emits objects with
.IR host ", " port ", " fingerprint ", " source ", " first_seen " and " updated_at
(or
.IR cid ", " bucket " and " fingerprint
for peers).
.
.\" ---------------------------------------------------------------------
.SH SYNCHRONISATION DIRECTIONS
.TP
.B bidirectional
Files are synced in both directions: local changes are pushed, remote changes
are pulled. This is the default and the only mode compatible with
.B \-\-force\-master
in p2p Mode.
.TP
.B upload\-only
Only local changes are pushed to the server/master.
Remote changes are ignored.
.TP
.B download\-only
Only remote changes are pulled from the server/master.
Local changes are ignored.
.
.\" ---------------------------------------------------------------------
.SH P2P MODE DETAILS
In
.B p2p Mode
.RB ( hsync " " p2p ),
clients on the same local network discover each other automatically
using
.B mDNS
(Bonjour/Avahi).
.
.P
One peer is dynamically elected as
.BR master .
The master is a transport hub: it serves the bucket and relays events,
but it does not decide conflicts by role. Slaves connect to the master
via HTTPS/WSS (always encrypted; self-signed certificates are generated
per device).
.
.P
A shared secret is set via the
.B HSYNC_P2P_KEY
environment variable and authenticates peers: only clients with the same
key can join the session. The key is also what authorizes writes — a keyless
p2p group is read-only, and a write-capable run is refused unless it is
download-only or passes
.B \-\-allow\-unauthenticated\-writes
on both sides.
.
.P
Cross-network discovery through a
.B boot/1
bootstrap node uses the same shared key when the node gates access: the client
derives a bucket token from
.B HSYNC_P2P_KEY
and presents it to a protected bucket or a private node, so the key must match
the key configured on the node.
.
.P
Use
.B \-\-group
to isolate multiple independent sync groups on the same network.
.
.\" ---------------------------------------------------------------------
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B HSYNC_SERVER
Sync-server endpoint: a bare
.RI host ,
.RI host : port ,
a bracketed IPv6 literal or
.RI [ IPv6 ]: port
(the HTTPS scheme and the default port 9753 are implied), or a full
.RI https://host[:port][/path]
URL (a base path is allowed only in this form). Alternative to the
.B hostname
argument of
.BR "hsync server" .
.TP
.B HSYNC_API_KEY
API key for authenticating with the server.
.TP
.B HSYNC_SERVER_TRUST
Sync\-server TLS trust policy:
.IR chain " (default), " ask ", " accept-new ", " strict " or " none .
Equivalent to
.BR \-\-server\-trust .
.TP
.B HSYNC_SERVER_FINGERPRINT
Comma-separated sync\-server certificate fingerprint(s) to pin (up to two,
.I sha256:<hex>
or bare hex). Equivalent to
.BR \-\-server\-fingerprint .
.TP
.B HSYNC_SERVER_TOFU
Trust the sync\-server certificate on first use (1 = on; default off).
Equivalent to
.BR \-\-server\-tofu .
.TP
.B HSYNC_SERVER_TRUST_FILE
File storing the trusted sync\-server fingerprints (default:
.IR $XDG_STATE_HOME/hsync/server_known_hosts.json ,
or
.IR ~/.local/state/hsync/server_known_hosts.json
when
.I XDG_STATE_HOME
is unset).
.TP
.B HSYNC_P2P_KEY
Shared secret for p2p mode peer authentication, and the credential that
authorizes writes: without it the group is read-only and a write-capable run
is refused unless it is download-only or the dangerous
.B \-\-allow\-unauthenticated\-writes
opt-in is explicit. With a bootnode it is also the group key the client derives
its bucket token from, required by a protected bucket or a private node.
.TP
.B HSYNC_NTP_HOSTS
Comma-separated list of SNTP servers, tried in order, used in p2p mode
(no server at startup) to measure the clock offset for chronological
conflict resolution with
.IR corrected_mtime
(default: pool.ntp.org,time.cloudflare.com,time.google.com). Entries may
carry a port override (
.IR host:port ).
.TP
.B HSYNC_MAX_CONCURRENT_TRANSFERS
Maximum number of concurrent file transfers (default:
.BR 5 ;
range: 1\(en20).
When auto-tuning is enabled, this value is derived from storage type,
bandwidth, and transfer-queue profile unless set explicitly.
.TP
.B HSYNC_AUTOTUNE
Enable auto-tuning of timeout, retry, and concurrency based on the
runtime environment (default:
.BR true ).
Set to
.B false
to disable auto-tuning and use static defaults.
.TP
.B HSYNC_HTTP_TIMEOUT
HTTP request timeout in seconds (1\(en300). When auto-tuning is enabled
and this is unset, the timeout is derived from measured network latency.
.TP
.B HSYNC_RECONNECT_DELAY
WebSocket reconnection delay in seconds (1\(en60). When auto-tuning is
enabled and this is unset, the delay is derived from RTT.
.TP
.B HSYNC_TRANSFER_RETRY_MIN_WAIT
Minimum per-file retry wait in seconds (exponential backoff floor).
When auto-tuning is enabled and this is unset, the value is derived
from RTT.
.TP
.B HSYNC_TRANSFER_RETRY_MAX_WAIT
Maximum per-file retry wait in seconds (exponential backoff ceiling).
When auto-tuning is enabled and this is unset, the value is derived
from RTT.
.TP
.B HSYNC_STABILITY_DELAY
Seconds a file must stay unchanged before it is uploaded
(default: 5; range: 1\(en60).
Already-idle files skip the wait.
.TP
.B HSYNC_RESYNC
Periodic resync interval in seconds (default:
.BR 300 ;
0 = disabled).
.TP
.B HSYNC_BOOTNODE
Optional bootnode endpoint for cross-network discovery: a bare hostname/IPv4, a
.RI HOST : PORT
pair, or a bracketed IPv6 literal (optionally
.RI [ IPv6 ]: port ).
No scheme or path. Unset keeps discovery on mDNS only. The QUIC port defaults to
443; an explicit
.B \-\-port
overrides a port embedded here.
.TP
.B HSYNC_BOOTNODE_FINGERPRINT
Comma-separated bootnode certificate fingerprint(s) to pin (up to two,
.I sha256:<hex>
or bare hex).
.TP
.B HSYNC_BOOTNODE_TOFU
Trust the bootnode certificate on first use (1 = on; default off).
.TP
.B HSYNC_BOOTNODE_TRUST
Bootnode TLS trust policy:
.IR ask " (default), " accept-new ", " strict " or " none .
Equivalent to
.BR \-\-bootnode\-trust .
.TP
.B HSYNC_BOOTNODE_TRUST_FILE
File storing the trusted bootnode fingerprints (default:
.IR $XDG_STATE_HOME/hsync/bootnode_known_hosts.json ,
or
.IR ~/.local/state/hsync/bootnode_known_hosts.json
when
.I XDG_STATE_HOME
is unset).
.TP
.B HSYNC_UPNP_ENABLED
Map the master TCP port with UPnP (true/false; default false = opt\-in only
with a bootnode).
.TP
.B HSYNC_P2P_LISTEN_PORT
Port to use when acting as p2p master (default: 0 = auto).
.TP
.B HSYNC_P2P_GROUP
Group name for p2p peer filtering (default: empty = no filter).
.TP
.B HSYNC_DISCOVERY_TIMEOUT
Seconds to wait for the first p2p peer (default:
.BR 0 ;
wait indefinitely, mirroring the server-mode default of retrying an
unreachable server forever).
.TP
.B HSYNC_NEVER_MASTER
Never become master in p2p mode (default:
.BR false ).
.TP
.B HSYNC_P2P_REQUIRE_PAIRING
Strict pairing: require out-of-band confirmation for first-seen master
certificates (default:
.BR false ).
.TP
.B HSYNC_P2P_PEER_DOWNLOAD
Enable exact-hash peer-assisted LAN full downloads (default:
.BR true ).
.TP
.B HSYNC_P2P_PEER_READ_CAP
Maximum concurrent peer-download response bodies served by a continuous slave
(advertised on the LAN handshake so requesters stay within it; saturation
answers 503 with a suggested retry delay) (default:
.BR 2 ;
range: 1\(en32).
.TP
.B HSYNC_P2P_PEER_SOURCES_MAX
Maximum unique peer devices attempted per file before the master fallback
(default:
.BR 3 ;
range: 1\(en8).
.TP
.B HSYNC_P2P_ALLOW_UNAUTHENTICATED_WRITES
Dangerously permit LAN mutations without a shared key (default:
.BR false ).
Reads remain available when this setting is false.
.TP
.B HSYNC_P2P_ALLOW_UNAUTHENTICATED
Explicitly acknowledge running P2P without a shared key (default:
.BR false ).
Peers are not authenticated and reads are open to the network.
.TP
.B HSYNC_ALLOW_DELETIONS
Accept the deletion risk without an interactive confirmation (default:
.BR false ).
.TP
.B HSYNC_IGNORE_DELETE
Do not propagate file deletions (default:
.BR false ).
.TP
.B HSYNC_COMPRESSION_ENABLED
Enable zstd compression for file transfers (default:
.BR true ).
.TP
.B HSYNC_DELTA_ENABLED
Enable rsync-style delta transfer for large files with small changes (default:
.BR true ).
When enabled, only changed blocks are transferred instead of the whole file,
significantly reducing bandwidth usage. Falls back to full transfer if delta
transfer fails or is not supported by the peer.
.TP
.B HSYNC_DELTA_MIN_FILE_SIZE
Minimum file size in bytes for delta transfer in server mode (default:
.BR 262144 ,
256 KB). Files smaller than this threshold are always transferred in full.
.TP
.B HSYNC_DELTA_MIN_FILE_SIZE_P2P
Minimum file size in bytes for delta transfer in p2p mode (default:
.BR 1048576 ,
1 MB). p2p mode uses a higher threshold because bandwidth savings are less
significant on fast local networks.
.TP
.B HSYNC_HEARTBEAT_INTERVAL
Heartbeat interval in seconds for p2p mode (default:
.BR 5 ;
range: 1\(en60). Governs how often a peer's mDNS presence is re-announced and how
often the discovery loop re-evaluates peer liveness.
.TP
.B HSYNC_BOOTNODE_REFRESH_INTERVAL
\fBboot/1\fR lease and query cadence in seconds (default:
.BR 30 ;
range: 1\(en300). Governs how often the client registers, refreshes its lease
and queries the bootnode for peers. Keep it inside the node's rate limits
(5 queries/min per IP and bucket; the protocol specifies a 30\(ens refresh).
.TP
.B HSYNC_PEER_TIMEOUT
Peer timeout in seconds for p2p mode (default:
.BR 15 ;
range: 3\(en600). A peer whose heartbeat has not been seen within this window is
considered dead and excluded from master election; the surviving peers then
elect a successor. Must be at least twice
.B HSYNC_HEARTBEAT_INTERVAL
so a single missed announce never triggers a needless re-election.
.TP
.B HSYNC_IGNORE_PATTERNS
Comma-separated extra gitignore-style patterns (layered on
.BR .hsyncignore ).
.TP
.B HSYNC_MASS_DELETE_GUARD
Enable/disable the mass-deletion safety guard (default:
.BR true ).
.TP
.B HSYNC_MASS_DELETE_THRESHOLD
Absolute number of deletions per cycle that trips the guard (default:
.BR 50 ;
0 = disabled).
.TP
.B HSYNC_MASS_DELETE_PERCENT
Percentage of local files whose deletion trips the guard (default:
.BR 50 ;
0 = disabled).
.TP
.B HSYNC_TOMBSTONE_TTL_DAYS
Days to retain deletion markers before garbage collection (default:
.BR 90 ;
0 = forever). Tombstones are not a recycle bin.
.TP
.B HSYNC_DEVICE_DIR
Directory holding the persistent device identity: the stable device ID
.RI ( device_id ),
the p2p keypair
.RI ( p2p_master_cert.pem ,
.IR p2p_master_key.pem ),
and the per-folder sync-state databases
.RI ( syncstate/<uuid>.db
plus
.IR syncstate/index.db ;
see
.BR HSYNC_STATE_DB ).
Default:
.IR $XDG_STATE_HOME/hsync/device ,
or
.IR ~/.local/state/hsync/device
when
.I XDG_STATE_HOME
is unset.
.TP
.B HSYNC_STATE_DIR
Installation state directory (default:
.IR $XDG_STATE_HOME/hsync ,
or
.IR ~/.local/state/hsync
when
.I XDG_STATE_HOME
is unset).
Used by the server for its per-bucket state; the client only shows the
resolved value in its verbose startup log and keeps its sync state under
the device dir instead (see
.BR HSYNC_DEVICE_DIR ).
.TP
.B HSYNC_STATE_DB
Explicit, process-wide sync-state database path. When set, the client opens
this single SQLite file for every synced folder instead of the per-folder
layout under the device dir. Useful for tests and manual isolation.
.TP
.B HSYNC_LOCKS_DIR
Directory holding the per-directory instance locks (one
.IR <sha256>.lock
file per synced directory). Resolution order:
.IR $HSYNC_LOCKS_DIR ,
then
.IR $XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/hsync/locks ,
then
.IR <device-dir>/locks .
.TP
.B HSYNC_P2P_PIN_FILE
File storing the pinned fingerprints of known p2p peers (default:
.IR $XDG_STATE_HOME/hsync/p2p_known_peers.json ,
or
.IR ~/.local/state/hsync/p2p_known_peers.json
when
.I XDG_STATE_HOME
is unset).
.
.\" ---------------------------------------------------------------------
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/hsync/hsync.conf
System-wide configuration file (read by the systemd service via
.IR EnvironmentFile ).
Uses KEY=VALUE format.
.TP
.I /var/log/hsync/hsync.log
Log file written by the systemd service
.RI ( StandardOutput / StandardError
append). Interactive runs log to the terminal unless
.B \-\-log\-file
is given.
.TP
.IR $XDG_STATE_HOME/hsync/device
(or
.IR ~/.local/state/hsync/device
when
.I XDG_STATE_HOME
is unset; override with
.BR HSYNC_DEVICE_DIR ).
Persistent device identity:
.I device_id
(the stable device ID),
.I p2p_master_cert.pem
and
.I p2p_master_key.pem
(the p2p keypair),
and
.IR syncstate/
(the per-folder SQLite databases
.IR <uuid>.db
plus the per-device
.IR index.db ).
.TP
.IR $XDG_STATE_HOME/hsync/p2p_known_peers.json
(or
.IR ~/.local/state/hsync/p2p_known_peers.json
when
.I XDG_STATE_HOME
is unset; override with
.BR HSYNC_P2P_PIN_FILE ).
Pinned fingerprints of known p2p peers (TOFU).
.TP
.IR $XDG_STATE_HOME/hsync/bootnode_known_hosts.json
(or
.IR ~/.local/state/hsync/bootnode_known_hosts.json
when
.I XDG_STATE_HOME
is unset; override with
.BR HSYNC_BOOTNODE_TRUST_FILE ).
Known-hosts store for bootnode certificate fingerprints.
.TP
.IR $XDG_STATE_HOME/hsync/server_known_hosts.json
(or
.IR ~/.local/state/hsync/server_known_hosts.json
when
.I XDG_STATE_HOME
is unset; override with
.BR HSYNC_SERVER_TRUST_FILE ).
Known-hosts store for sync\-server certificate fingerprints.
.TP
.IR $XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/hsync/locks
(or
.IR <device-dir>/locks
without a runtime dir; override with
.BR HSYNC_LOCKS_DIR ).
Per-directory instance locks (one
.IR <sha256>.lock
file per synced directory).
.TP
.I .hsyncignore
Per-directory ignore file (gitignore syntax).
Placed in the root of the synced directory.
.TP
.I .hsynckeep
Marker file that forces a directory to be kept even if it would otherwise
be empty after synchronization.
.TP
.I .hsyncfolder
Folder-identity marker (UUIDv4). Causal versions and deletion markers live in
a per-folder SQLite database under the device dir
.RI ( $HSYNC_DEVICE_DIR/syncstate/<uuid>.db ),
not inside the synced directory.
.
.\" ---------------------------------------------------------------------
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
Basic sync with a remote server:
.RS
.EX
hsync server server.example.com \-b photos
.EE
.RE
.TP
Sync a specific local directory:
.RS
.EX
hsync server server.example.com \-b documents \-p ~/Documents
.EE
.RE
.TP
Continuous (default) mode:
.RS
.EX
hsync server server.example.com \-b projects
.EE
.RE
.TP
One-shot sync:
.RS
.EX
hsync server server.example.com \-b projects \-\-once
.EE
.RE
.TP
Dry-run preview (no changes made):
.RS
.EX
hsync server server.example.com \-b backup \-n
.EE
.RE
.TP
p2p peer-to-peer mode (the shared key authorizes writes):
.RS
.EX
HSYNC_P2P_KEY=mysecret hsync p2p \-b shared
.EE
.RE
.TP
p2p mode with a specific group:
.RS
.EX
HSYNC_P2P_KEY=mysecret hsync p2p \-b shared \-\-group home
.EE
.RE
.
.SS Bootnode discovery
Discover peers across networks through a boot/1 bootstrap node. The first
contact shows the certificate fingerprint and asks for confirmation (like
.BR ssh (1)),
then remembers it:
.PP
.EX
hsync p2p boot.example.net \-b shared
.EE
.PP
Non-interactive deployments accept the first sighting explicitly, or pin a
fingerprint the operator published out of band:
.PP
.EX
hsync p2p boot.example.net \-b shared \-\-bootnode\-tofu
hsync p2p boot.example.net \-b shared \-\-bootnode\-fingerprint sha256:FINGERPRINT
.EE
.PP
Read a node's fingerprint without trusting it, pin it, and manage the known
hosts (like
.B ssh\-keyscan (1)
and
.BR ssh\-keygen \-R ):
.PP
.EX
hsync trust bootnode fingerprint boot.example.net
hsync trust bootnode add boot.example.net sha256:FINGERPRINT
hsync trust bootnode list
hsync trust bootnode remove boot.example.net
.EE
.PP
Authenticate to a private node or a protected bucket (the key must match the
node's group-keys entry):
.PP
.EX
HSYNC_P2P_KEY=mysecret hsync p2p boot.example.net \-b shared
.EE
.PP
Manage the p2p known-peers store (like
.B ssh\-keyscan (1)
and
.BR ssh\-keygen \-R ):
.PP
.EX
hsync trust peer add AbCdEfGhIjKlMnOpQrStU sha256:FINGERPRINT \-\-bucket photos
hsync trust peer list
hsync trust peer remove AbCdEfGhIjKlMnOpQrStU \-\-bucket photos
.EE
.PP
Pin a self-signed sync\-server certificate (verify the fingerprint out of band
first), or accept the first sighting non\-interactively:
.PP
.EX
hsync trust server fingerprint server.example.com
hsync trust server add server.example.com sha256:FINGERPRINT \-\-port 9753
hsync server server.example.com \-b photos \-\-server\-trust strict
hsync server server.example.com \-b photos \-\-server\-tofu
.EE
.
.TP
Backup mode (upload only, never delete remote files):
.RS
.EX
hsync server server.example.com \-b backup \-\-sync\-direction upload\-only \-\-ignore\-delete
.EE
.RE
.TP
Bandwidth-limited sync:
.RS
.EX
hsync server server.example.com \-b media \-\-limit\-upload 2MB
.EE
.RE
.TP
Reverse proxy on the standard HTTPS port (the default port is 9753):
.RS
.EX
hsync server server.example.com \-\-port 443 \-b photos
.EE
.RE
.
.\" ---------------------------------------------------------------------
.SH SIGNALS
.TP
.B SIGINT ", " SIGTERM
Graceful shutdown. The running daemon will complete any in-progress
transfers before exiting.
.
.\" ---------------------------------------------------------------------
.SH EXIT STATUS
One-shot runs
.RB ( \-\-once )
return these codes (see
.IR docs/scheduling.md ).
Continuous/daemon runs typically exit 0 or 1.
.TP
.B 0
Synchronisation completed with no anomalies (also a successful dry-run),
or a persistent daemon exited cleanly.
.TP
.B 1
Fatal error: invalid configuration, unreachable server, authentication
failure, directory lock held, or an unexpected exception.
.TP
.B 2
The cycle completed but some transfers failed. Re-runnable.
.TP
.B 3
The mass-deletion guard skipped unconfirmed deletions this cycle.
.TP
.B 4
Causal conflicts were resolved by preserving
.I *_conflicted_copy_*
files.
.TP
.B 5
P2P one-shot: no peer/master found within the discovery timeout (a lone
client exits instead of serving as master).
.
